    {
      "id": "Hstk",
      "code_hash": "22724afde73eaa7e44487294a7f6f582",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"4-forward-backward-state-probabilities-at-every-position\">4. Forward-backward: state probabilities at every position</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The forward variable accumulates evidence left-to-right:</span>\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||[\\alpha_t(k) = \\Big[\\sum_j \\alpha_{t-1}(j)\\,A(j,k)\\Big]\\, b_k(x_t)||]</marimo-tex><span class=\"paragraph\">and the backward variable <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\beta||)</marimo-tex> does the mirror-image\ncomputation right-to-left. Multiplying them together and\nnormalizing gives the posterior <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(P(\\text{state}_t \\mid\n\\text{all observations})||)</marimo-tex> \u2014 this is exactly what lets one noisy\npoint borrow strength from its neighbors on <em>both</em> sides.\nEverything below runs in log-space, since these products\nunderflow almost immediately otherwise.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "nWHF",
      "code_hash": "55a7d8d90bf07adfa1afb60fb6531822",
      "outputs": [],
      "console": []
    },
    {
