    {
      "id": "ROlb",
      "code_hash": "2e716a69f9a52fce7f50b060e73114fd",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"5-viterbi-the-single-best-path\">5. Viterbi: the single best path</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Forward-backward gives per-position probabilities; Viterbi\ninstead finds the <em>one</em> most likely sequence of states for the\nwhole track, by swapping the sum in the forward recursion for a\nmax:</span>\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||[\\delta_t(k) = \\max_j\\big[\\delta_{t-1}(j)\\,A(j,k)\\big]\\, b_k(x_t)||]</marimo-tex><span class=\"paragraph\">A backpointer array records which <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(j||)</marimo-tex> won at each step, so once\nwe reach the end we can walk back through the winning path. This\nis the one you'd actually use to call discrete segments.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
